            },
            "description": "### What it does\n🔒 `users:manage`. Updates a user's name, role, and/or active flag using **optimistic concurrency**: `version` is required and must equal the row's current version, otherwise the write is rejected. All fields except `version` are optional.\n\n### Request body\n```json\n{ \"name\": \"Jane Senior Editor\", \"roleId\": \"<uuid>\", \"active\": true, \"version\": 1 }\n```\n\n### Returns\n**200 OK** — the updated user, with `version` incremented by 1.\n\n### Errors\n- `400` validation (e.g. missing `version`)\n- `401` · `403`\n- `404` user not found\n- `409` version conflict (someone else updated it first)"
          },
